$\begin{align}
7^2\cdot 7^6&=7^{2+6}
\\\\
&=7^{8}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $x^m\cdot x^n=x^{m+n}$. Note that the powers have the same base.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
7^2\cdot 7^6&=\underbrace{7\cdot 7}_\text{2 times}\cdot\underbrace{7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7}_\text{6 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7\cdot 7}_\text{8 times}
\\\\
&=7^{8}
\end{align}$
